open-fdd's rules implement fault conditions from ASHRAE Guideline 36.

Changes made in the port (see each rule's docstring):
  * All thresholds converted from °F / in.w.c. / cfm / gpm / psi to SI
    (°C, Pa, m³/s, L/s). Inputs are role columns already converted to SI
    by agent_commercial.semantics.
  * Rules and gates use ARVIS canonical point roles.
  * When no run-proof point exists (fan status/speed/command, pump or
    chiller status), gated rules are SKIPPED instead of assuming the
    equipment was running.
  * Site-specific thresholds with no universal default (e.g. CHW-4 flow
    limit) must be configured; the rule is skipped otherwise.
  * Sensor-validation results invalidate dependent samples rather than
    letting a failed sensor raise a mechanical fault.
  * Economizer / outside-air rules only apply when the equipment's
    commissioned design says it has an economizer.
  * Each rule uses its own declared confirmation delay. (In open-fdd 4.4.7
    a shared 5-minute `confirm_min` slider overrides every rule's declared
    delay.)
  * FC13 full-cooling threshold 0.95 (open-fdd ships 0.01 while labelling
    it "GL36 99%"); FC13/FC14 treat a unit with no OA-damper point as having
    no economizer, so "valve closed" is the coil-inactive state.
  * FC1 requires the VFD speed signal (with only a status point open-fdd
    reduces "fan at full speed" to "fan running").
  * SV-RANGE mixed-air high limit 55 °C instead of 110 °F, for 100%-outdoor-
    air units in hot climates.
  * CHW-NOLOAD-1 redefined (chiller on while every mapped cooling valve is
    closed); VAV-2 replaced by ZONE-SETBACK-1 (cooling setback); DC-DT-1 new.
  * Rules that need a minimum data span (SCHED-247: 24 h) SKIP until they
    have it.

Parity with the original is tested in tests/test_fdd_parity.py against
open-fdd 4.4.7 (requirements-dev-fdd.txt).
